:FOUND: 2026-09-11
:PRIORITY: highest open risk
:END:

- *What*: =/bisos/asc/web/bin/= holds 8 =airflow-*.pcs= files --- the
  predecessor installation, from before =bisos.airflow= existed as a
  package. They come *first* on PATH:

  #+begin_example
  airflow-webserver-sysd.pcs  -> /bisos/asc/web/bin/airflow-webserver-sysd.pcs
  airflow-sbom.pcs            -> /bisos/asc/web/bin/airflow-sbom.pcs
  airflow-cbs.pcs             -> /bisos/asc/web/bin/airflow-cbs.pcs
  #+end_example

- *Why it matters*: those copies =diff= as pre-migration --- zero
  occurrences of =User=airflow= or =airflowAcctEnvSetup=. Invoking any of
  them *by bare name* re-materializes the **root-era** units over the top of
  the migrated installation, silently and apparently successfully.
- *Why nothing broke*: every invocation during the migration used an
  explicit repo path. Deliberate, but not a durable safeguard.
- *Action*: retire the =/bisos/asc/web/bin/= airflow copies, or ensure the
  package wins on PATH.
----- Results: ------
Done 2026-10-01. Retired the copies; the PATH alternative was not
available, because =bisos.airflow= is not pip-installed and so nothing
from =py3/bin/= is on PATH.

- *CBM pointer* (Mohsen, =bro_rawBisos= commits =a102cb7=, =11c6fec=,
  =5ad1cd8=): the planted leaf
  =sys/cbm/collective/hereWeb/airflow/cbmProc.spcs= has
  =cbsSpec="/bisos/git/bxRepos/bisos-pip/airflow/py3/bin/airflow-cbs.pcs"=,
  an absolute path that PATH order cannot affect. The leftover symlink
  =sys/cbm/airflow-cbs.pcs= was removed.
- *Stale copies deleted* (Mohsen): all 9 =airflow-*= files in
  =bisos/asc/web/bin/= (=bisos/asc= commit =addaad4=; the set included
  =airflow-assemble.cs=, so 9 files, not 8). Also removed
  =airflow-here-dns.pcs= and =airflow-wvd.pcs= from
  =/bisos/venv/py3/bisos3/bin/=. Verified: =which -a= finds no
  =airflow-*.pcs= on PATH.
- *No damage occurred*: the installed =airflow-*.service= units all carry
  =User=airflow= + =EnvironmentFile=/etc/default/airflow= and were last
  written 2026-09-11/12.
- *Docs in =bro_rawBisos=* (Claude): updated the references that still
  presented =/bisos/asc/web/bin/= as current. These were in
  =AI-DevStatus.org=, =AI-Activity.org= and
  =bro_rawBisosPlatform/README.org=. DONE TODO results in its
  =AI-WorkPlan.org= were kept as history, with dated notes added.
  Uncommitted.
- *Out of scope, same pattern*: the =nginx= and =reactPlus= CBM leaves
  still have =cbsSpec= under =/bisos/asc/web/bin/=. Those files are not
  airflow.
- *Pitfall*: =/bisos/git/anon/bxRepos/bxObjects/bro_rawBisos= is a stale
  clone (last pulled 2026-08-26) that still shows the old =cbsSpec=. The
  live tree is the =/bisos/git/auth/= clone.


