----- Results: ------
2026-10-01. *Airflow-Usage panel* (the authoritative "what =bisos.airflow=
does"): =py3/panels/bisos.airflow/airflowUsage/_nodeBase_/fullUsagePanel-en.org=.

- *New node =airflowUsage/=*: skeleton copied from =serverSetup/= with its
  self-paths renamed. The panel holds the package-level content of the old
  =AI-Usage.org=, re-verified against source and the live units and updated
  for the airflow-user installation:
  - =airflow= account, =/opt/airflow=, =/etc/default/airflow=, and why
    =EXECUTION_API_SERVER_URL= matters;
  - the PostgreSQL metadata DB with peer auth;
  - five units, including =dag-processor=;
  - CBS/CBM with an absolute =cbsSpec=;
  - nginx+DNS exposure;
  - executor and cross-venv scope, and a commands table.

  Corrected an old claim: the package *does* choose the backend
  (PostgreSQL). It does not choose the executor.
- *Top-level panel* =_nodeBase_/fullUsagePanel-en.org=: the blank
  "Overview Comes Here." is replaced with a short overview and a
  child-panel table. Each child is marked authoritative, being updated,
  or aspirational, and the overview points to =airflowUsage=.
- *Gaps and maturity* moved to =AI-DevStatus.org= under "Known gaps and
  maturity", together with new findings: stale sbom =readme= text, the
  PATH reach of bare =.pcs= names, and =/etc/default/airflow= being
  write-once. That last one is harmless on this host, because
  =airflow.cfg= sets both Airflow 3 URLs.
- *=AI-Usage.org= removed* (=git rm=). The downstream consumer
  =site-status-scripts/airflow/AI-Activity.org= now =@=-imports the
  =airflowUsage= panel via =/bisos/git/bxRepos/...=, and its 4 textual
  references point at the panel. Two of its instance facts that 4.3 made
  false were also corrected: the backend is PostgreSQL, not SQLite
  (verified in =airflow.cfg=), and the =/bisos/asc/web/bin/= PATH caveat no
  longer applies.
- *Pending (Mohsen, in Blee)*: run Update Buf Dblocks on the new panel and
  on the parent panel and =ftoProc.sh=, so that =airflowUsage= appears in
  the navigators and =nodesList=.

